# Docker build-context exclusions. The Dockerfile sits beside this file, so the context
# root is THIS directory and everything above it - the legacy estate, docs, diagrams,
# vendor archives and the .git tree - is already outside the context. Docker cannot escape
# the context root, so no parent-directory pattern appears here; wanting one means the
# build was invoked from the wrong directory.
#
# .dockerignore is not .gitignore. A bare extension rule matches the context root only,
# so every extension rule is written twice: bare for the root and with a "**/" prefix for
# every deeper level. Dropping the "**/" form silently reopens the hole it closes, which
# for the credential rules is a security regression and not merely a context-size one.
# A trailing slash prunes a whole subtree, and the last matching rule wins.
#
# Excluding too little bloats the context, breaks layer caching and risks a host-compiled
# class reaching the image instead of one the builder stage compiled under -Xlint:all
# -Werror. Excluding too much silently removes a build input, so the foot of this file
# re-includes every required input by name as a tripwire against a future blanket rule.

# Build output, in every location a tool might write it.
target/
**/target/
build/
out/
bin/
dist/
*.jar
*.JAR
**/*.jar
**/*.JAR
*.war
*.WAR
**/*.war
**/*.WAR
*.ear
*.EAR
**/*.ear
**/*.EAR
*.class
*.CLASS
**/*.class
**/*.CLASS
*.exec
*.EXEC
**/*.exec
**/*.EXEC
*.hprof
*.HPROF
**/*.hprof
**/*.HPROF

# The wrapper ships as scripts only. The wrapper directory itself is never pruned: a
# re-inclusion cannot resurrect a file beneath a pruned directory, and the builder stage
# needs the descriptor to resolve Maven.
.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar
.mvn/.develocity/
.mvn/.gradle-enterprise/

# Maven plugin residue. Complete file names, so none can match the wrapper descriptor.
dependency-reduced-pom.xml
.flattened-pom.xml
pom.xml.releaseBackup
pom.xml.versionsBackup
pom.xml.next
pom.xml.tag
release.properties
buildNumber.properties

# Gate evidence and scan output. Reproducible from a clean checkout plus one build, so it
# is never an image input.
dependency-check-report.*
**/dependency-check-report.*
.dependency-check/
**/.dependency-check/
dependency-check-data/
**/dependency-check-data/
surefire-reports/
**/surefire-reports/
failsafe-reports/
**/failsafe-reports/
jacoco*.exec
**/jacoco*.exec
site/
**/site/
test-output/
**/test-output/

# Credential material. The image resolves every secret from the environment at run time,
# so none of this may ever enter a layer - a file copied into an image stays in that
# layer even if a later stage deletes it.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

