# Runtime and diagnostic output. The container logs to stdout, so no log file is ever an
# image input.
*.log
*.LOG
*.log.*
**/*.log
**/*.LOG
**/*.log.*
logs/
**/logs/
hs_err_pid*
**/hs_err_pid*
replay_pid*
**/replay_pid*
heapdump*
**/heapdump*
core
core.[0-9]*
**/core.[0-9]*

# Required build inputs, re-included by name. Nothing above matches them; because the last
# matching rule wins, these lines also neutralise a future blanket rule added above.
!pom.xml
!mvnw
!.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.properties

# The committed Spring profiles - ALL FOUR. The production profile holds no secret value, only
# unresolved environment references.
#
# application-test.yml appears TWICE in this module, under src/main/resources and under
# src/test/resources, and both are named deliverables. The one below is the packaged copy: it is the
# complete definition of the profile and it is what lets the BUILT ARTEFACT be started with
# --spring.profiles.active=test. Omitting it from the build context, as an earlier revision did,
# silently withdrew that capability from the image while leaving the file in the repository looking
# delivered. The suite-only copy is re-included further down for a different reason.
!src/main/resources/application.yml
!src/main/resources/application-local.yml
!src/main/resources/application-test.yml
!src/main/resources/application-prod.yml
!src/main/resources/logback-spring.xml
!src/main/resources/banner.txt

# Schema migrations - all four, across the two sibling locations that carry them - and the externalised
# validation lookup tables. The single recursive re-include below covers both: db/migration/schema
# holds V1 and V2 and is resolved by every profile, db/migration/seed holds V3 and V4 and is resolved
# by the local and test profiles only, and their shared parent holds no script at all.
#
# The two seed scripts are included deliberately: an image is run under the local and test profiles
# as well as production, so they must be present on the image class path for those profiles to find
# them. Production does not reach them, and it does not rely on their absence from the image to
# achieve that - it resolves the schema location alone, with FlywayConfig refusing it the seed location
# outright and additionally refusing a ceiling that reaches a seed version, and
# ProductionSeedRejectionCallback refusing a start-up whose database has ever had one applied.
# Excluding them from the image would be a control that only looks like one, because it would break
# local and test instead. See docs/decision-log.md DL-127.
!src/main/resources/db/migration/**
!src/main/resources/lookup/**

# Test resources and byte-parity fixtures. The builder stage packages with tests skipped, so
# these are not inputs to the packaging step itself; they are sent so that the same context can
# run the suite inside the builder stage without a second, differently-shaped context, and so a
# byte-parity fixture can be compared against output produced by the image rather than only by a
# workstation. This is the SUITE-ONLY copy of the test profile; it specialises the packaged copy
# re-included above, and on the test class path it shadows it. Both are required.
!src/test/resources/application-test.yml
!src/test/resources/fixtures/input/**
!src/test/resources/fixtures/expected/**
